DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ddhhccpplleeaasseedd is a dynamic host configuration protocol (DHCP) daemon for
     clients.  If an interface has the AAUUTTOOCCOONNFF44 flag set (auto configuration
     is enabled), ddhhccpplleeaasseedd sends requests for IP configuration information
     from a DHCP server, such as dhcpd(8), and uses that information to con‐
     figure the relevant interface.

     See hostname.if(5) and ifconfig(8) on how to enable auto configuration on
     an interface.

     ddhhccpplleeaasseedd monitors network interface states (interface going up or down,
     auto configuration enabled or disabled, etc.) and sends requests when
     necessary.  A running ddhhccpplleeaasseedd can be controlled with the
     dhcpleasectl(8) utility.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Do not daemonize.  If this option is specified, ddhhccpplleeaasseedd will
             run in the foreground and log to _s_t_d_e_r_r.

     --ff _f_i_l_e
             Specify an alternative configuration file.

     --nn      Configtest mode.  Only check the configuration file for validity.

     --ss _s_o_c_k_e_t
             Use an alternate location for the default control socket.

     --vv      Produce more verbose output.  Multiple --vv options increase the
             verbosity.

